Links and sources

As you read History Tracers, you will notice that certain words, names, and numbers appear as clickable links. These links connect the text to the sources that support it.

A link is shown in a different color and usually underlined. When you hover over it, the cursor changes to a hand. Click the link and its source opens on the right side of the screen.

The right side is organized into four categories. Primary sources are original documents and records from the time of the events. References are books, articles, and websites. Religious references are sacred texts. Social media includes videos and posts.

Each link sends its source to the matching category. Try it now. Click a link in any text and watch where the source appears.

With these four categories, you can always trace the origin of what you are reading.
